      "markdown": "# Array operations\n\nUse the state player to explore **25 examples**. Each example starts with `[30, 10, 20, 10]`; the upper row is the original and the lower row is the result. Gold marks changed or selected slots. Empty results show **empty**.\n\n**Read:** length, indexed access, search (`indexOf`), membership (`includes`), and traversal.\n\n**Change:** update, insert, delete, append/push, pop, prepend/unshift, shift, swap, reverse, sort, fill, resize, and clear.\n\n**Create a new sequence:** slice (start included, end excluded) and concatenate. The original row remains unchanged, including for sort and reverse.\n\nIndices are zero-based. Search returns the first exact match or `-1`; it never converts strings to numbers. Empty pop/shift returns ∅. Sorting accepts homogeneous numbers or strings. Invalid indices are errors. Arrays are limited to 256 cells.\n\nDirect access and update touch one slot. Middle insertions and deletions shift a suffix; prepend and shift move the whole remainder. Append and pop affect the end. Compare the two rows to see these differences.",
